// THE CODE ON THE DIALS, remembered between sessions.
//
// Three dials, two bits each, in bits 0-5: dial 1 in 0-1, dial 2 in 2-3, dial 3 in 4-5. Four
// letters per dial is exactly two bits, so the whole code is six bits and there is no invalid
// state to guard against - every value 0-63 is a code somebody could have dialled, which is why
// the lookup answers "nothing happens" rather than erroring.
//
// scope=perm because RuneScape's rings remember where you last went, and a player who hops
// Zanaris -> Edgeville every login should not re-dial DKR each time.
//
// protect=no because [if_button,...] reads and writes it. The tribal door's varp says the same
// thing for the same reason (%handelmort_traps_disabled, quest_totem), and so do skill_guide.varp
// and game_options.varp: a protected varp is unreadable from a button trigger.
[fairy_ring_dial]
scope=perm
protect=no
